package sandbox

import b "github.com/plimsollmark/plimsoll/internal/boundary"

// dockerClaims is what the docker provider's SmokeTest (docker_smoke.go) proves, claim by
// claim, and why it does not prove the rest. SmokeTest records each claim as its check
// passes and fails when the record differs from this declaration; docs/isolation-tiers.md
// prints it.
var dockerClaims = b.Declare(b.Declaration{
	Provider: "docker",
	Source:   "sandbox/docker_smoke.go",
	Startup:  "It starts throwaway containers under the exact lockdown a run gets, one for each configured image, and checks from inside what each can do; then it runs a snippet and a project's runner as runs do.",
	Entries: map[b.Claim]b.Entry{
		b.WritablePlaces: {Steps: []string{"smokeProbe", "smokeGuestGuard"},
			How: "a write to the root filesystem must fail, and a write is tried at every mount point: only the promised <dfn>*tmpfs*</dfn> mounts (filesystems held in memory) may accept one, `/tmp` and `/dev/shm`, and `/work` in a project image. That is what exists when code starts, and the code cannot add a place of its own later, under `runc` or gVisor: making one needs a user namespace of its own (a private view of the system in which it acts as administrator) and a mount in it, and the guest guard refuses both (see `guest-guard`, whose check is also this claim's); under `runc` the shipped seccomp profile refuses them too."},
		b.WritableBounds: {Steps: []string{"smokeProbe"},
			How: "in the container's own list of mounted filesystems, each promised mount must be a tmpfs of exactly its configured size, marked `noexec` (a file written there cannot be started or loaded as a program by its path; code a run places in memory is not stopped by it, so `noexec` is a second layer, not the wall; and since the guest guard refuses the code a folder of its own, under `runc` and gVisor alike, there is no unmarked folder for it to copy a program into) and `nosuid`."},
		b.LoopbackOnly: {Steps: []string{"smokeProbe"},
			How: "the container's own list of network interfaces must be loopback alone, which is what having no network means inside a container."},
		b.NoEgress: {Not: "with loopback the only interface (checked above), no packet has a way out, and the docker suite's tests try connections (`TestDockerRunHasNoEgress`)."},
		b.GuestUser: {Steps: []string{"smokeProbe"},
			How: "every user and group ID the kernel states for the test's process, and every supplementary group, must be the guest user's: a runtime could accept `--user` and run the code as someone else."},
		b.NoCapabilities: {Not: "the lockdown passes `--cap-drop ALL` and `no-new-privileges` to docker."},
		b.SeccompFilter:  {Not: "[Preflight](trainers/glossary.html#preflight), the provider's check of its configuration, checks each configured seccomp profile file, and under `runc` every container gets that profile or docker's default; under gVisor no host profile is applied, since gVisor filters requests in its own kernel. The guest guard's own filter, which the test does prove in force under both, is the `guest-guard` claim."},
		b.GuestGuard: {Steps: []string{"smokeGuestGuard"},
			How: "every command plimsoll starts in a container, the code's and plimsoll's own, starts behind the guest guard: a small program of plimsoll's, carried inside plimsolld and mounted read-only into each container (an operator's own image needs nothing added for it), that puts a seccomp filter on itself before anything else runs; every program started after it keeps the filter, and none can take it off. In a [session](trainers/glossary.html#session) the container's first process is the guest guard too, in place of docker's own init (`--init`), which docker started outside it: it stays as process 1 behind its own filter, starts the session's main process and collects every process that ends in the container, and a session does not open unless process 1 is that program. The filter refuses with \"Operation not permitted\" the requests that make a namespace (`unshare`, `clone` with a namespace flag, `setns`), that mount or change the root (`mount`, `umount2`, `pivot_root`, `chroot` and the newer mount calls), and tracing (`ptrace`, `process_vm_writev`), so a debugger or `strace` does not work in the sandbox; it answers `clone3` and every request numbered above the newest it was reviewed against with \"Function not implemented\", and ends a process that makes a request through the 32-bit or x32 entry. In each image the test starts a check program of plimsoll's exactly as a run starts the code, and requires the guest guard's answers, under `runc` and under gVisor alike: a request answered in a way only the guest guard's filter answers it, then a user namespace, `clone3`, tracing and a mount refused, then an ordinary request that works; in the image sessions run, it starts the check a second time in a session's shape, with the guest guard as process 1, and under gVisor it requires both processes' `Seccomp` lines in `/proc` to say a filter is on them. Not every one of those answers tells the guest guard from no guest guard: without it a mount is refused anyway (the code holds no capabilities), and under `runc` with the shipped profile so are tracing and a user namespace. What proves the filter is on the code's program is the first answer, which only the guest guard's filter gives, and under gVisor also the namespace and tracing answers, which gVisor without the guest guard allows; the ordinary request proves the filter does not refuse everything. That the filter refuses each request it names is proved by the guest guard's own bytes instead: the guest guard program is named by its SHA-256, [Preflight](trainers/glossary.html#preflight) compares the file every container mounts with the copy inside plimsolld, and plimsoll's tests hold the filter in those bytes to its table. Not covered: the test runs under the default seccomp profile only, never under the variant a run whose grant sets `sdk_env` gets ([seccomp.md](seccomp.md#the-second-profile-runs-whose-grant-sets-sdk_env)): under gVisor no host profile applies, and under `runc` the variant plimsoll derives changes only sockets, but an operator's own variant that ended a process for a request the guest guard makes, instead of refusing it, would be found at the first such run, which fails, not at startup; a machine type with no tested build of the guest guard (only x86-64 has one), where the provider refuses to serve, and a docker daemon, `DOCKER_DEFAULT_PLATFORM` or image for another machine than plimsolld's own, which Preflight refuses for the same reason; and code that puts a program in memory (`memfd_create`) and starts it from there, which no filter of this kind stops. The guest guard is a second layer in front of the code, not the sandbox's wall: the wall is the container under `runc`, or gVisor's kernel."},
		b.ProcessLimit: {Steps: []string{"smokeProbe", "proveSandboxPidsLimit"},
			How: "the container's `pids.max` must equal the configured limit, because a runtime can accept `--pids-limit` without applying it. Under gVisor the container sees an emulated copy of that file that always reads `max`, while gVisor applies the limit to the sandbox's <dfn>*cgroup*</dfn> (the kernel's record of a group of processes' limits) on the host, so there the test reads the host's copy instead, from a container it starts for that."},
		b.MemoryLimit: {Not: "the lockdown passes `--memory`, with `--memory-swap` equal to it so there is no swap."},
		b.CPULimit:    {Not: "the lockdown passes `--cpus`."},
		b.FixedResolver: {Steps: []string{"smokeProbe"},
			How: "the container's `/etc/resolv.conf` must be plimsoll's fixed file byte for byte, since docker writes the host's search domains and name servers there even with no network."},
		b.ClosedEnvironment: {Not: "plimsoll's own programs start under `env -i` with a fixed PATH, and code gets the verified image's environment and nothing else; a test with an image whose `NODE_OPTIONS` loads a hook holds that split (`TestDockerImageEnvReachesOnlyGuestProcesses`)."},
		b.ControlChannel: {Steps: []string{"smokeNativeHelper", "smokeGuard", "smokeRunner"},
			How: "in each project image the project runner, plimsoll's native helper at `/usr/local/libexec/plimsoll-helper`, must be a regular file, root's and writable by no one else, whose SHA-256 is that of the copy inside plimsolld (the hash is computed inside the image, so this proves the image is the one plimsoll built, not that a hostile image could not lie); the library `/usr/local/lib/plimsoll-runner-guard.so` must be a file, and a program started as a [session](trainers/glossary.html#session) starts its sweep, its quiesce and the relay of each [cell](trainers/glossary.html#cell), with that library loaded first to make it <dfn>*non-dumpable*</dfn> (no other program of the same user may open its descriptors or read its memory), must be listed by the kernel as no longer the guest user's (its `/proc/<pid>/environ` is root's) and its descriptors refused to a process of that user, since a loader that cannot find the library starts the program without it and without a word; and the runner is started as runs start it, and a project step's opens of the runner's plan and report descriptors and of its memory must be refused."},
		b.NoHostShare: {Not: "the lockdown mounts nothing of the host's but plimsoll's fixed resolver file and the guest guard program, both read-only, and, for a grant, the run's own socket to plimsolld."},
		b.TierInside:  {Not: "the kernel tier rests on Preflight's reading that the docker daemon registers `runsc` as a program named `runsc`. Under gVisor the test reads the first line of the kernel log, but only for the startup log, since a line like it is easy to forge."},
		b.SetupReadBack: {Steps: []string{"SmokeTest"},
			How: "Preflight reads the one local docker daemon it is bound to: the configured runtime must be registered there, every configured image must be present by its content ID and declare no `VOLUME` (and, with `SANDBOX_REQUIRE_PINNED_IMAGES=1`, be <dfn>*pinned*</dfn>: named by its <dfn>*digest*</dfn>, a hash of its content that names exactly those bytes), and every configured seccomp profile must be a file that agrees with the others; the containers above start those exact content IDs."},
		b.RunPath: {Steps: []string{"smokeSnippet", "smokeRunner"},
			How: "a snippet must run as runs run it and print what it should, and in each project image the runner must complete a one-step project."},
		b.DeadlineKill: {Not: "a run's teardown force-removes its container, which ends every process in it."},
		b.OutputCap:    {Not: "plimsolld reads each stream of a container through a capped buffer of its own."},
		b.GrantSocket: {Steps: []string{"smokeProbe"},
			How: "the first container mounts a throwaway host Unix socket exactly as a grant's socket to plimsolld is mounted, and must reach it; gVisor refuses one unless registered with `--host-uds=open`."},
		b.Languages: {Steps: []string{"probeLanguages"},
			How: "each interpreter is run once in the project image; node must answer, since a session's programs and the granted-run forwarder are node, and only the languages that answer are stated."},
		b.Teardown: {Not: "every container is started with `--rm` and a label with its expiry, which the orphan sweep removes when a container outlives its run."},
	},
})
